# Links lychee must not fail on. One reason per entry; nothing here without one.
#
# The repository slug is real (`ubberkid/kraken-hub`), so github.com and
# ubberkid.github.io links are checked like any other. Issue and discussion
# links are written absolute for the same reason — GitHub's fork-relative
# `../../issues/…` form is meaningless as a filesystem path and used to have to
# be excluded here, which is exactly how a wrong-depth link once hid from CI.

# --- deep links that require a signed-in CAM ---------------------------------
# cam-redirect hands off to a desktop application. There is no page behind it to
# fetch, and it answers a bot with a redirect to a login wall.
^https://cam-redirect\.nzxt\.com
^https://cam-beta-redirect\.nzxt\.com

# --- hosts that refuse automated requests ------------------------------------
# NZXT's support Zendesk answers 403 to anything without a browser fingerprint;
# the article is real and was read during research.
^https://support\.nzxt\.com
# x.com serves an SPA shell and a 400 to non-browser clients.
^https://x\.com
# YouTube endpoints referenced in why-not-extraction.md are the *subject* of that
# document's measurements; several are expected to answer 403 by design.
^https://www\.youtube\.com/youtubei
^https://.*\.googlevideo\.com
